# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# PRODUCTION-READY LEAD CAPTURE SYSTEM — Environment Variables
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# 
# This file documents all environment variables for the contact form & lead
# capture system. Copy to .env.local and fill in your secrets.
#
# IMPORTANT: Never commit .env.local to git — it contains secret API keys
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# REQUIRED: EMAIL SENDING (Resend)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Without these, the form won't send any emails at all.

# API Key from https://resend.com/api-keys
# Get one free at: https://resend.com (free tier available)
# Format: re_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
RESEND_API_KEY=re_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# Verified sender email in Resend
# Must match a verified domain in your Resend account
# Examples: noreply@yourdomain.com, contact@yourdomain.com
# For testing: onboarding@resend.dev (test-only)
RESEND_FROM_ADDRESS=noreply@yourdomain.com

# Your personal/business email inbox
# All lead notifications go here with full details
# Must be a real, working email address
OWNER_EMAIL=your-email@gmail.com

# Required in production for distributed contact-form rate limiting.
# Create a free Redis database at https://upstash.com, then copy the REST URL
# and token from the database REST API settings.
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=https://your-redis.upstash.io
UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=your-token-here

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OPTIONAL: TELEGRAM INSTANT ALERTS
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Skip these if you don't want real-time Telegram notifications.
# Highly recommended for quick lead response.

# Telegram Bot Token
# Get from @BotFather on Telegram: https://t.me/BotFather
# Steps:
#   1. Message @BotFather with "/newbot"
#   2. Follow prompts to create a bot
#   3. Copy the token shown at the end
# Format: 1234567890:ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZabcdefgh
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=1234567890:ABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZabcdefgh

# Telegram Chat ID where alerts are sent
# Get by:
#   1. Start your bot on Telegram
#   2. Send it any message
#   3. Visit: https://api.telegram.org/bot<TOKEN>/getUpdates
#   4. Find "chat":{"id": in the response (negative number for groups)
# For private chats: positive number
# For groups/channels: negative number
TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID=-1234567890123

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# PUBLIC: SITE CONFIGURATION
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# These are safe to expose in the browser (NEXT_PUBLIC prefix).

# Your production website URL (used in emails and redirects)
# Important for email templates and verification
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://yourdomain.com

# Calendly booking link (for hero section)
# Leave empty to hide the booking button
NEXT_PUBLIC_CALENDLY_URL=https://calendly.com/your-username/audit

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OPTIONAL: ANALYTICS (architecture-ready, not configured by default)
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Uncomment when you activate Google Analytics 4 or Microsoft Clarity
# No tracking will happen without these — the system is ready to go, just needs IDs

# Google Analytics 4 ID
# Create at: https://analytics.google.com/
# Property ID format: G-XXXXXXXXXX
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_ID=G-XXXXXXXXXX

# Microsoft Clarity ID
# Create at: https://clarity.microsoft.com/
# Project ID format: numeric string
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CLARITY_ID=xxxxxxxxxx

# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# QUICK START CHECKLIST
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# [ ] 1. Create Resend account & get API key
#        → https://resend.com/api-keys
#
# [ ] 2. Verify your domain or use onboarding@resend.dev for testing
#        → https://resend.com/domains
#
# [ ] 3. Fill in RESEND_API_KEY, RESEND_FROM_ADDRESS, OWNER_EMAIL
#
# [ ] 4. (Optional) Setup Telegram bot notifications
#        → Message @BotFather, get token & chat ID
#
# [ ] 5. Copy .env.example to .env.local
#        → npm run copy:env  (if script exists)
#        → OR manually create .env.local with these values
#
# [ ] 6. Test locally: npm run dev
#        → Go to http://localhost:3000/#contact
#        → Submit test form
#        → Check OWNER_EMAIL inbox
#
# [ ] 7. Deploy to Vercel
#        → Push to GitHub
#        → Add these secrets to Vercel project settings
#        → Redeploy
#
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# DEPLOYMENT NOTES (Vercel)
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# In Vercel Project Settings → Environment Variables, add:
#   • RESEND_API_KEY (secret)
#   • RESEND_FROM_ADDRESS
#   • OWNER_EMAIL (secret)
#   • TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN (secret, if using Telegram)
#   • TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID (if using Telegram)
#   • NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL
#   • NEXT_PUBLIC_CALENDLY_URL (optional)
#   • NEXT_PUBLIC_GA_ID (optional)
#   • NEXT_PUBLIC_CLARITY_ID (optional)
#
# Vercel automatically loads .env vars for:
#   • Development: .env.local (git-ignored)
#   • Production: Variables set in dashboard
#
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# SECURITY BEST PRACTICES
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
# ✓ Never commit .env.local (it's in .gitignore)
# ✓ Server-only variables never reach the browser
# ✓ All form data is validated server-side
# ✓ Rate limiting blocks spam (5 requests per minute per IP)
# ✓ Honeypot field catches bots automatically
# ✓ Email addresses are HTML-escaped in templates
# ✓ Telegram token is never exposed to client
# ✓ WhatsApp fallback is only used if Resend fails
#
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
